    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-f/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The sum to infinity of a geometric progression is four times as large as its second term. a) Show that the common ratio of the series is 1 2 . ( ) 4 It is further given that the sum of the first four terms of the progression is 5760. b) Find the first term of the progression. ( ) 3 The sum of the first k terms of the progression is three less than its sum to infinity. ( ) 4 c) Use algebra to determine the value of  k .\" style=\"--madas-width:580.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
