      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-f/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"= 4(3072)(1/2) . = 6144 We need Sk = S∞−3. Thus 3072(1 −0.5k)/(1 −0.5) = 6141, giving 3072(1 −0.5k) = 6141(0.5), 1 −0.5k = 2047/2048 and 0.5k = 1/2048. The tail after k terms is 6144(1/2)k = 3. [B1] Therefore 2k = 2048 [A1] = 211 by inspection: Alternatively, k log(1/2) = log(1/2048) and k = log(1/2048)/ log(1/2) . = 11\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-f/q9-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Hence k = 11 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:205.3px\"></figure>",
